IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa19-regulative.l4: the duties of Part 25 (ss 859K, 859Q, 860, 862, 868, 871, 877, 878, 880, 892) that name a party and a time, as regulative rules.
-- A regulative rule is run with #TRACE (see coa19-tests-regulative.l4). On the stable binary a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT, so the outcome of a
-- trace is read by eye and recorded in NOTES.md; EVERY duty here is ALSO encoded as a decision function that the tests assert:
--   ss 859K(2), 859K(3): `s 859K(2)(a) the person gave the registrar notice within 7 days`, `s 859K(3) the person must, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice` (coa19-a1-after)
--   ss 860(1), 862(2), 878(1), 880(2): `s 860(4) ...`, `s 862(4) ...`, `s 878(4) ...`, `s 880(3) ...` and `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` (coa19-ch1-requirements, coa19-ch2-scotland, coa19-nouns)
--   s 868(3)(b): `s 868(3)(b) the last day on which the registrar must cause the other copy ...` (coa19-ch1-requirements)
--   ss 859Q(3), 877(3), 892(3): `s 859Q(5) an offence is committed` and its twins (coa19-a1-records, coa19-ch1-registrar, coa19-ch2-scotland)
-- WITHIN counts days in this file (the clock of each #TRACE is days from the start of the duty). The text says "within 7 days of the order" or "before the end of the period allowed": the clock
-- here starts on the day of the order, of the creation of the charge, or of the acquisition (the period of s 870 and s 886 starts the day after: 21 days from the day after is a clock of 21 days).
-- No actor, deadline or consequence is invented: where the text gives no period (s 859K(3), "on so ceasing") the rule has no WITHIN.

DECLARE `s 859K party` IS ONE OF
    `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment`
    `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge`
    `s 868 the registrar`

DECLARE `s 859K act` IS ONE OF
    `s 859K gives notice to the registrar of the order or appointment`
    `s 859K gives notice to the registrar that the receiver or manager has ceased to act`
    `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar`
    `s 859Q gives notice to the registrar of the place where the documents are kept`
    `s 868 sends the other copy and the certificate of registration to the company`

-- s 859K(2)(a): within 7 days of the order or of the appointment, give notice to the registrar of that fact; default is an offence (s 859K(6)).
-- src:11737 | (2) The person must, within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers—
-- src:11738 | (a) give notice to the registrar of that fact, and
@ref s 859K(2)(a) The person must, within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers, give notice to the registrar of that fact (src:11737-11738)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 859K(2)(a) the person must give notice to the registrar within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment`
    MUST `s 859K gives notice to the registrar of the order or appointment`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment` BECAUSE "no notice to the registrar within 7 days of the order or of the appointment: default, an offence under section 859K(6)"

-- s 859K(3): on ceasing to act, give notice. The text states no period, so there is no WITHIN.
-- src:11742 | (3) Where a person appointed receiver or manager of a company's property or undertaking under powers contained in an instrument ceases to act as such a receiver or manager, the person must, on so ceasing—
-- src:11743 | (a) give notice to the registrar of that fact, and
@ref s 859K(3) the person must, on so ceasing, give notice to the registrar of that fact (src:11742-11743)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 859K(3)(a) the person must, on ceasing to act, give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment`
    MUST `s 859K gives notice to the registrar that the receiver or manager has ceased to act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment` BECAUSE "no notice to the registrar on ceasing to act: default, an offence under section 859K(6)"

-- s 871(1): within 7 days of the order or of the appointment, give notice of the fact to the registrar; default is an offence (s 871(4)).
-- src:11958 | (1) If a person obtains an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property, or appoints such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument, he shall within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers, give notice of the fact to the registrar.
@ref s 871(1) he shall within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers, give notice of the fact to the registrar (src:11958-11958)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 871(1) the person must give notice of the fact to the registrar within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment`
    MUST `s 859K gives notice to the registrar of the order or appointment`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment` BECAUSE "no notice to the registrar within 7 days of the order or of the appointment: default, an offence under section 871(4)"

-- s 860(1): the company delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument before the end of the period allowed for registration (21 days beginning with the day after the day the charge is created:
-- a clock of 21 days from the day of creation); failure is an offence (s 860(4)).
-- src:11845 | (1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with the instrument (if any) by which the charge is created or evidenced, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 860(1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with the instrument, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:11845-11845)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument within the period allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge`
    MUST `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` BECAUSE "the particulars and instrument were not delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration: an offence under section 860(4)"

-- s 862(2), (3): the same duty for a charge existing on property the company acquires (21 days from the day after the acquisition is completed).
-- src:11877 | (2) The company must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a certified copy of the instrument (if any) by which the charge is created or evidenced, to the registrar for registration.
-- src:11878 | (3) Subsection (2) must be complied with before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 862(2) The company must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a certified copy of the instrument, to the registrar for registration (3) before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:11877-11878)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 862(2) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge`
    MUST `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` BECAUSE "the particulars and certified copy were not delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration: an offence under section 862(4)"

-- s 878(1) (Scotland): as s 860(1).
-- src:12020 | (1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a copy certified as a correct copy of the instrument (if any) by which the charge is created or evidenced, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 878(1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a copy certified as a correct copy of the instrument, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:12020-12020)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 878(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge`
    MUST `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` BECAUSE "the particulars and certified copy were not delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration: an offence under section 878(4)"

-- s 880(2) (Scotland): as s 862(2).
-- src:12054 | (2) The company must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a copy (certified to be a correct copy) of the instrument (if any) by which the charge was created or is evidenced, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 880(2) The company must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with a copy certified to be a correct copy of the instrument, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:12054-12054)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 880(2) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge`
    MUST `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` BECAUSE "the particulars and certified copy were not delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration: an offence under section 880(3)"

-- s 868(3)(b): not later than 7 days from the date of delivery of the copies, the registrar sends the other copy and the certificate to the company. A duty of the registrar,
-- encoded for what the company in the seat is owed (the seat is never an official).
-- src:11921 | (3) On delivery of copies under this section, the registrar shall—
-- src:11922 | (a) register one of them in accordance with section 869, and
-- src:11923 | (b) not later than 7 days from that date of delivery, cause the other copy together with a certificate of registration under section 869(5) to be sent to the company against which judgment was given.
@ref s 868(3)(b) the registrar shall, not later than 7 days from that date of delivery, cause the other copy together with a certificate of registration under section 869(5) to be sent to the company (src:11921-11923)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 868(3)(b) the registrar must send the other copy and the certificate to the company within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 868 the registrar`
    MUST `s 868 sends the other copy and the certificate of registration to the company`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 868 the registrar` BECAUSE "the other copy and the certificate of registration were not sent to the company within 7 days of the date of delivery of the copies"

-- ss 859Q(3), 877(3), 892(3): the company gives notice to the registrar of the place where the documents are kept, and of any change. The text gives no period for the notice; the offence
-- (ss 859Q(5), 877(5), 892(5)) arises "if default is made for 14 days". The rule therefore carries WITHIN 14 for the offence, counted from the day the duty arises (fork F-P2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:11829 | (3) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:11830 | (a) of the place at which the documents are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:11831 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:11832 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 859Q(3) The company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in that place (src:11829-11832)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 859K party` `s 859K act`
`s 859Q(3) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge`
    MUST `s 859Q gives notice to the registrar of the place where the documents are kept`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` BECAUSE "no notice to the registrar of the place where the documents are kept, in default for 14 days: an offence under section 859Q(5), 877(5) or 892(5)"
